{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates strong structural foundations but suffers from critical D96A EANCOM INVOIC incompleteness. The model is missing ~60% of mandatory segments (only 3-4 present vs. 15-20 required), lacks all qualifier distinctions that define EDIFACT semantics, and contains fundamental flattening errors that merge distinct business concepts. The GLN constraint is also incorrectly typed as xsd:string rather than enforcing numeric n13 format.",
  "completeness_score": 0.35,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "BGM_BeginningOfMessage",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "MANDATORY. The BGM segment (C002/1001 document name code, C106/1004 document number, 1225 message function) is the foundational identifier of the invoice type and number. Without this, you cannot distinguish between an invoice (380), credit note (381), or debit note (383). Your :HeaderSection class is too", "owl_reviewed_length": 26612, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

