{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a solid foundational understanding of EDIFACT structure but suffers from critical flattening errors, missing qualifier distinctions, and incomplete D96A INVOIC coverage. Most critically, it models only ~40% of required segments and fails to distinguish between semantically different instances of the same segment type (e.g., NAD+BY vs NAD+SU). The GLN constraint is also insufficiently strict.",
  "completeness_score": 0.42,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "NAD_Buyer",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "NAD+BY (Buyer) must be modeled as a distinct subclass of NAD_NameAndAddress. The current generic NAD class violates EANCOM's requirement that Buyer identification is mandatory and has specific GLN validation rules. Without this distinction, the ontology cannot enforce that every invoice MUST have exactly one Buyer."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name":", "owl_reviewed_length": 24441, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

